WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.988
Step six prints each
wave with its rollback.

2
00:00:02.988 --> 00:00:08.053
Wave 1 is Mail Automation, with a rollback
owner, and its rollback re-enables the

3
00:00:08.053 --> 00:00:13.587
legacy credential, reverts the configuration
and removes the federated credential.

4
00:00:13.587 --> 00:00:21.013
Wave 2 holds svc hrsync, svc intranet, a
managed service account and Payroll Export.

5
00:00:21.013 --> 00:00:24.431
svc intranet is there because
its owner re-platforms it

6
00:00:24.431 --> 00:00:27.999
to the group managed service
account the matrix proposes.

7
00:00:27.999 --> 00:00:30.487
And the wave's rollback owner is empty.

8
00:00:30.487 --> 00:00:34.138
That's the N P I M A T oh eight finding.

9
00:00:34.138 --> 00:00:39.010
Notice the delegated managed account's
rollback is the undo command from Microsoft

10
00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:42.421
Learn's delegated managed
service account documentation,

11
00:00:42.421 --> 00:00:45.275
and the superseded account
is kept, never deleted.

12
00:00:45.275 --> 00:00:48.900
Step seven reads the
Workload I D Premium scope.

13
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:52.111
Six single-tenant app
registrations can be covered by

14
00:00:52.111 --> 00:00:55.250
Conditional Access today,
and four after conversion.

15
00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:59.049
Payroll Export is one that
leaves: its owner's decision moves

16
00:00:59.049 --> 00:01:03.000
it to a managed identity, and
managed identities aren't covered.

17
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.213
Step eight runs every test:
five hundred thirteen pass.

18
00:01:07.213 --> 00:01:10.630
Then delete the output, which
names accounts and owners.
